course: dictionary
lesson: 278
title: Amend and making amends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Amend has two meanings. The first is about writing: to amend a rule, a law or a draft is to change it a little so it is more correct or better. The second is about saying sorry: to make amends is to do something good to show you are sorry for a wrong you did.
explain: Look at the words around amend to find its meaning. «The school council decided to amend the playground rules.» Rules can be changed to make them better, so amend means to change something a little to improve it. Try the swap: "The school council decided to change the playground rules a little." It still makes sense.
explain: «Making amends can be a kind thing you do, not only money.» The clues are kind thing and not only money. Making amends means doing something good, and it can be time, work or kindness. Amends is a noun here, and it only appears in the phrase make amends.
fact: Amend is a verb: amend, amends, amended, amending.
fact: «Amend» means to change something a little to correct or improve it.
fact: «Make amends» means to do something good to show you are sorry for a wrong you did.
fact: Making amends can be work as well as money, like painting a porch you damaged.
fact: Coming clean or owning up means admitting what you did; making amends means doing something to fix the harm.
exercise: «The class voted to amend the rule about homework.» What does amend mean here? | *To change it a little to make it better | To read it out loud | To throw it away completely | To copy it into a new book
exercise: Sam broke Maya's glasses, so he read to her every day until she could see well again. What is this an example of? | Teasing a friend | Owning a pet | *Making amends | Writing a new law
exercise: «Standing up for someone who is teased is a strong way to make amends.» What does make amends mean? | *To do something good to show you are sorry for a wrong | To buy a new coat for the teacher | To argue until you win | To forget what happened
test: Ravi drew on the library wall. Which choice is a way to make amends? | *Helping to clean the wall and tell the librarian what he did | Hiding the marks under a chair | Drawing more pictures on the wall | Telling nobody and going home
test: A writer wants to amend her story before she sends it. What does she do? | Deletes the whole story | *Changes a few parts to improve it | Sends it without reading it | Reads it aloud only once
exam: Mia admits she broke the window and then helps pay for the repair. What is Mia doing? | Amending a law | *Making amends | Hiding the broken glass | Teasing a friend
